<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60044" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρῐτ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>, ὁ, voc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κριτή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hippon.
					118
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρίνω</span>):—<i>judge,
				umpire</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				397
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.160
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν πέντε κριτῶν γούνασι κεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					229
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τῶν ἀληθῶν</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοξαστής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.94
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κριταὶ ἀπὸ τοῦ ἴσου</span>,
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγωνισταί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.37
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν . . λεγομένων μὴ κακοὺς κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.120
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					16.21
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				65a
			</span></i>; at Athens, usu. of <i>the judges in the poetic
			contests</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1224
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				445
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.21
			</span></i>; rarely, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικαστής</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Demad.
				3
			</span></i>: so metaph. in <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.232
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα τὰ στοιχεῖα κριτὴν
			εἴληφε</span>, i. e. each element has found favour with some
			philosopher, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>de An.</u>
				405b8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1337a42
			</span></i>; of the <u>Judges</u> of Israel, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jd.</u>
				2.16
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δοθείς</span>,
			= Lat. <i>judex datus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				1195.1
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίλεκτος
			κ.</span>, =
			<i>judex selectus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				567.10
			</span></i> (Attalia, <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐνυπνίων</span>
			<i>interpreter</i> of dreams, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				226
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κριτάς: ὀδόντας</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραντήρ</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
